IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc18-soira-notice`

-- ccc18-soira-itoa.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 490.029111 to 490.02915 (persons transferred to Canada under the International
-- Transfer of Offenders Act: exemption, variation and termination orders, and the notice before release). Part agent ccc18; layer 1. It imports
-- `ccc18-soira-notice` (bands, the end-of-obligation type, date helpers). The International Transfer of Offenders Act is not among the sources: whatever
-- it provides (Form 1, section 36.1 obligations, the durations of section 36.2) is taken as an input. Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE of a type):
-- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (not covered); see the header of `ccc18-soira-notice` and NOTES.md.

§ `Sections 490.029111 to 490.02915 -- International Transfer of Offenders Act`

§ `490.029111 Application for exemption order`

-- src:10502 | International Transfer of Offenders Act
-- src:10503 | Application for exemption order
-- src:10504 | 490.029111 (1) A person who is subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act may apply to a court of criminal jurisdiction for an order exempting them from the obligation within one year after the day of their transfer to Canada under that Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029111(1) (src:10502-10504)
GIVEN `they are subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of their transfer to Canada under that Act` IS A DATE
      `the day on which they apply for an order exempting them from the obligation` IS A DATE
      `the application is made to a court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029111(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` MEANS
    IF NOT `they are subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act may apply"
    ELSE IF `the day on which they apply for an order exempting them from the obligation` AT MOST `the day of their transfer to Canada under that Act`
            OR `the day on which they apply for an order exempting them from the obligation` GREATER THAN `s 490.021(1) one year after the day` `the day of their transfer to Canada under that Act`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may apply to a court of criminal jurisdiction for an order exempting them from the obligation within one year after the day of their transfer to Canada under that Act"
         ELSE IF `the application is made to a court of criminal jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is to apply "to a court of criminal jurisdiction"

-- src:10505 | Exemption order
-- src:10506 | (2) The court shall make an exemption order if it is satisfied that the person has established that
-- src:10507 | (a) there is no connection between the obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act; or
-- src:10508 | (b) the impact of the obligation on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, is grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029111(2) (src:10505-10508)
DECLARE `s 490.029111(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.029111(2) make an exemption order`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029111(2) (src:10505-10508)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the person has established that there is no connection between the obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of the obligation on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, is grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029111(2) the court shall make an exemption order` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the person has established that there is no connection between the obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`
       OR `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of the obligation on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, is grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall make an exemption order if it is satisfied that the person has established that" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029111(2) (src:10505-10508)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.029111(2) action`
`s 490.029111(2) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.029111(2) make an exemption order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court was satisfied of a ground and did not make an exemption order"

-- src:10509 | Factors
-- src:10510 | (3) In determining whether to make an exemption order, the court shall consider
-- src:10511 | (a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation;
-- src:10512 | (b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics;
-- src:10513 | (c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim;
-- src:10514 | (d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person;
-- src:10515 | (e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence;
-- src:10516 | (f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person; and
-- src:10517 | (g) any other factors that the court considers relevant.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029111(3) (src:10509-10517)
DECLARE `s 490.029111(3) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.029111(3)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation`
    `s 490.029111(3)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics`
    `s 490.029111(3)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim`
    `s 490.029111(3)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person`
    `s 490.029111(3)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence`
    `s 490.029111(3)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person`
    `s 490.029111(3)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant`
    `s 490.029111(3) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029111(3) (src:10509-10517)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether to make an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
      factor IS A `s 490.029111(3) factor`
      `the court considers the matter relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029111(3) the court shall consider the factor` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court is determining whether to make an exemption order`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In determining whether to make an exemption order, the court shall consider" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE CONSIDER factor
         WHEN `s 490.029111(3)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.029111(3)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.029111(3)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.029111(3)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.029111(3)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.029111(3)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.029111(3)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (g): "any other factors that the court considers relevant" is itself in the list
         WHEN `s 490.029111(3) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)` THEN IF `the court considers the matter relevant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only factors "that the court considers relevant" are added by paragraph (g)

-- src:10518 | Reasons for decision
-- src:10519 | (4) The court shall give reasons for its decision.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029111(4) (src:10518-10519)
DECLARE `s 490.029111(4) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.029111(4) give reasons for its decision`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029111(4) (src:10518-10519)
GIVEN `the court has made a decision under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029111(4) the court shall give reasons for its decision` MEANS
    IF `the court has made a decision under subsection (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "The court shall give reasons for its decision"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029111(4) (src:10518-10519)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.029111(4) action`
`s 490.029111(4) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.029111(4) give reasons for its decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not give reasons for its decision"

-- src:10520 | Removal of information from database
-- src:10521 | (5) If the court makes an exemption order, it shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029111(5) (src:10520-10521)
DECLARE `s 490.029111(5) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.029111(5) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029111(5) (src:10520-10521)
GIVEN `the court makes an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029111(5) the court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an exemption order` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court makes an exemption order" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029111(5) (src:10520-10521)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.029111(5) action`
`s 490.029111(5) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.029111(5) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court made an exemption order and did not order the removal of the information"

§ `490.029112 Application for variation order`

-- src:10522 | Application for variation order
-- src:10523 | 490.029112 (1) A person who is subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act may, within one year after the day of their transfer to Canada under that Act, apply to a court of criminal jurisdiction for an order to vary the duration of the obligation if
-- src:10524 | (a) the obligation applies for life under subsection 36.2(3) of that Act; and
-- src:10525 | (b) none of the offences in question listed in the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of that Act have an equivalent criminal offence with a maximum term of imprisonment for life provided for in Canadian law.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029112(1) (src:10522-10525)
GIVEN `they are subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of their transfer to Canada under that Act` IS A DATE
      `the day on which they apply for an order to vary the duration of the obligation` IS A DATE
      `the application is made to a court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) the obligation applies for life under subsection 36.2(3) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) none of the offences in question listed in the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of that Act have an equivalent criminal offence with a maximum term of imprisonment for life provided for in Canadian law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029112(1) the person may apply for a variation order` MEANS
    IF NOT `they are subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act may"
    ELSE IF `the day on which they apply for an order to vary the duration of the obligation` AT MOST `the day of their transfer to Canada under that Act`
            OR `the day on which they apply for an order to vary the duration of the obligation` GREATER THAN `s 490.021(1) one year after the day` `the day of their transfer to Canada under that Act`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within one year after the day of their transfer to Canada under that Act, apply to a court of criminal jurisdiction for an order to vary the duration of the obligation"
         ELSE IF `the application is made to a court of criminal jurisdiction`
                 AND `(a) the obligation applies for life under subsection 36.2(3) of that Act`
                 AND `(b) none of the offences in question listed in the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of that Act have an equivalent criminal offence with a maximum term of imprisonment for life provided for in Canadian law`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is given "if (a) the obligation applies for life under subsection 36.2(3) of that Act; and (b) none of the offences in question"

-- src:10526 | Variation order
-- src:10527 | (2) The court shall make the variation order if it is satisfied that the person has established that the offences in question listed in that Form 1 do not demonstrate, or do not form part of, a pattern of behaviour showing that the person presents an increased risk of reoffending by committing a crime of a sexual nature.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029112(2) (src:10526-10527)
DECLARE `s 490.029112(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.029112(2) make the variation order`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029112(2) (src:10526-10527)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the offences in question listed in that Form 1 do not demonstrate, or do not form part of, a pattern of behaviour showing that the person presents an increased risk of reoffending by committing a crime of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029112(2) the court shall make the variation order` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the offences in question listed in that Form 1 do not demonstrate, or do not form part of, a pattern of behaviour showing that the person presents an increased risk of reoffending by committing a crime of a sexual nature`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall make the variation order if it is satisfied that the person has established that the offences in question" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029112(2) (src:10526-10527)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.029112(2) action`
`s 490.029112(2) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.029112(2) make the variation order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court was satisfied of the ground and did not make the variation order"

-- src:10528 | Variation of duration
-- src:10529 | (3) If the court makes a variation order, it shall set out the duration of the obligation in the order, which shall be determined by applying paragraphs 36.2(2)(a) and (b) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act to the offence in question listed in that Form 1 whose equivalent criminal offence has the longest maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029112(3) (src:10528-10529)
GIVEN `the court makes a variation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the duration that paragraphs 36.2(2)(a) and (b) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act give for the offence in question listed in that Form 1 whose equivalent criminal offence has the longest maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law, by section 36.2 of that Act` IS A MAYBE `s 490.022(3) end of the obligation`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 490.022(3) end of the obligation`
`s 490.029112(3) the duration of the obligation set out in the variation order` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court makes a variation order`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court makes a variation order, it shall set out the duration of the obligation in the order"
    ELSE `the duration that paragraphs 36.2(2)(a) and (b) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act give for the offence in question listed in that Form 1 whose equivalent criminal offence has the longest maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law, by section 36.2 of that Act`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): paragraphs 36.2(2)(a) and (b) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act are not among the sources, so their answer is an input

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029112(3) (src:10528-10529)
DECLARE `s 490.029112(3) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.029112(3) set out the duration of the obligation in the variation order`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029112(3) (src:10528-10529)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.029112(3) action`
`s 490.029112(3) the duty of the court to set out the duration` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.029112(3) set out the duration of the obligation in the variation order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court made a variation order and did not set out the duration of the obligation in it"

