-- src:10532 | Notification
-- src:10533 | (5) The court shall cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of a variation order made under this section.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029112(5) (src:10532-10533)
DECLARE `s 490.029112(5) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.029112(5) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of a variation order made under this section`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029112(5) (src:10532-10533)
GIVEN `the court makes a variation order under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029112(5) the court shall cause the notification to be given` MEANS
    IF `the court makes a variation order under this section` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "of a variation order made under this section"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029112(5) (src:10532-10533)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.029112(5) action`
`s 490.029112(5) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.029112(5) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of a variation order made under this section`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court made a variation order and did not cause the notification to be given"

§ `490.029113 Appeal`

-- src:10534 | Appeal
-- src:10535 | 490.029113 (1) The Attorney General or the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order may appeal from a decision under subsection 490.029111(2) or 490.029112(2) or (3) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may
-- src:10536 | (a) dismiss the appeal; or
-- src:10537 | (b) allow the appeal and order a new hearing, quash or amend the exemption order or variation order or make an order that may be made, as the case may be, under subsection 490.029111(2) or section 490.029112.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029113(1) (src:10534-10537)
DECLARE `s 490.029113(1) appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.029113(1) the Attorney General`
    `s 490.029113(1) the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order`
    `s 490.029113(1) another person`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029113(1) (src:10534-10537)
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 490.029113(1) appellant`
      `the decision appealed from is a decision under subsection 490.029111(2) or 490.029112(2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground of appeal raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029113(1) the appeal may be brought` MEANS
    IF appellant EQUALS `s 490.029113(1) another person` OR (NOT `the decision appealed from is a decision under subsection 490.029111(2) or 490.029112(2) or (3)`) OR (NOT `the ground of appeal raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Attorney General or the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order may appeal from a decision under subsection 490.029111(2) or 490.029112(2) or (3) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10535 | 490.029113 (1) The Attorney General or the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order may appeal from a decision under subsection 490.029111(2) or 490.029112(2) or (3) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may
-- src:10536 | (a) dismiss the appeal; or
-- src:10537 | (b) allow the appeal and order a new hearing, quash or amend the exemption order or variation order or make an order that may be made, as the case may be, under subsection 490.029111(2) or section 490.029112.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029113(1) (src:10535-10537)
DECLARE `s 490.029113(1) thing the appeal court does` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.029113(1) dismiss the appeal`
    `s 490.029113(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing`
    `s 490.029113(1) quash the exemption order or variation order`
    `s 490.029113(1) amend the exemption order or variation order`
    `s 490.029113(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.029111(2) or section 490.029112`
    `s 490.029113(1) another thing`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029113(1) (src:10535-10537)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 490.029113(1) thing the appeal court does`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029113(1) the appeal court may do it` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `s 490.029113(1) dismiss the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.029113(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.029113(1) quash the exemption order or variation order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.029113(1) amend the exemption order or variation order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.029113(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.029111(2) or section 490.029112` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.029113(1) another thing` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) allow the appeal and order a new hearing, quash or amend the exemption order or variation order or make an order that may be made"

-- src:10538 | Removal of information from database
-- src:10539 | (2) If an appeal court makes an exemption order, it shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029113(2) (src:10538-10539)
DECLARE `s 490.029113(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.029113(2) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029113(2) (src:10538-10539)
GIVEN `an appeal court makes an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029113(2) the appeal court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` MEANS
    IF `an appeal court makes an exemption order` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an appeal court makes an exemption order" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029113(2) (src:10538-10539)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.029113(2) action`
`s 490.029113(2) the duty of a court of appeal` MEANS
    PARTY `a court of appeal`
    MUST `s 490.029113(2) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a court of appeal` BECAUSE "the appeal court made an exemption order and did not order the removal of the information"

§ `490.029114 Requirements relating to notice`

-- src:10540 | Requirements relating to notice
-- src:10541 | 490.029114 (1) If an appeal court quashes an exemption order, it shall cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision and shall cause the person who applied for the order to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029114(1) (src:10540-10541)
GIVEN `an appeal court quashes an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029114(1) the appeal court shall cause the notification and the information to be given` MEANS
    IF `an appeal court quashes an exemption order` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an appeal court quashes an exemption order" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029114(1) (src:10540-10541)
DECLARE `s 490.029114(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.029114(1) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision`
    `s 490.029114(1) cause the person who applied for the order to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029114(1) (src:10540-10541)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.029114(1) action`
`s 490.029114(1) the duty of the appeal court to cause the Commissioner and the Attorney General to be notified` MEANS
    PARTY `a court of appeal`
    MUST `s 490.029114(1) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a court of appeal` BECAUSE "the Commissioner and the Attorney General were not notified of the decision"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029114(1) (src:10540-10541)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.029114(1) action`
`s 490.029114(1) the duty of the appeal court to cause the person to be informed of the sections` MEANS
    PARTY `a court of appeal`
    MUST `s 490.029114(1) cause the person who applied for the order to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a court of appeal` BECAUSE "the person who applied was not informed of the sections"

