§ `490.02912 Application for termination order`

-- src:10544 | Application for termination order
-- src:10545 | 490.02912 (1) A person who is subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act may apply to a court of criminal jurisdiction for a termination order unless they are also subject to an obligation under section 490.019 or 490.02901 or under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act — or to an order under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act — that began later.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02912(1) (src:10544-10545)
GIVEN `they are subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are also subject to an obligation under section 490.019 or 490.02901 or under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act, or to an order under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act, that began later` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to a court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02912(1) the person may apply for a termination order` MEANS
    IF `they are also subject to an obligation under section 490.019 or 490.02901 or under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act, or to an order under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act, that began later`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may apply to a court of criminal jurisdiction for a termination order unless they are also subject to an obligation under section 490.019 or 490.02901"
    ELSE IF `they are subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act` AND `the application is made to a court of criminal jurisdiction`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act may apply to a court of criminal jurisdiction"

-- src:10546 | Time for application — one offence
-- src:10547 | (2) The person may apply for a termination order if the following period has elapsed since the sentence was imposed or the verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder was rendered:
-- src:10548 | (a) five years if the maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence is two or five years;
-- src:10549 | (b) 10 years if the maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence is 10 or 14 years; or
-- src:10550 | (c) 20 years if the maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence is life.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02912(2) (src:10546-10550)
GIVEN `the maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence` IS AN Imprisonment
      `the day on which the sentence was imposed or the verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder was rendered` IS A DATE
      `the day on which they apply for a termination order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02912(2) the person may apply for a termination order, the period since sentence having elapsed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 490.022(3) the band of the maximum term of imprisonment` `the maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence`
    WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of two or five years` THEN `the period of` 5   -- (a)
    WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of 10 or 14 years` THEN `the period of` 10   -- (b)
    WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of life` THEN `the period of` 20   -- (c)
    WHEN `s 490.022(3) any other maximum term, or none stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names maximum terms of two, five, 10, 14 years and life only
    WHERE
        `the period of` n MEANS
            IF `the day on which they apply for a termination order` AT LEAST `s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which the sentence was imposed or the verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder was rendered` n
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The person may apply for a termination order if the following period has elapsed" (fork F5: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:10551 | More than one offence
-- src:10552 | (3) If more than one offence is listed in the copy of the Form 1 that was delivered under subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, the person may apply for a termination order if 20 years have elapsed since the sentence was imposed, or the verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder was rendered, for the most recent offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02912(3) (src:10551-10552)
GIVEN `more than one offence is listed in the copy of the Form 1 that was delivered under subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the sentence was imposed, or the verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder was rendered, for the most recent offence` IS A DATE
      `the day on which they apply for a termination order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02912(3) the person may apply for a termination order, 20 years having elapsed since the most recent offence` MEANS
    IF `more than one offence is listed in the copy of the Form 1 that was delivered under subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act`
       AND `the day on which they apply for a termination order` AT LEAST `s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which the sentence was imposed, or the verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder was rendered, for the most recent offence` 20
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If more than one offence is listed in the copy of the Form 1 that was delivered under subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, the person may apply for a termination order if 20 years have elapsed" (fork F5)

-- src:10553 | Absolute discharge
-- src:10554 | (3.1) Despite subsections (2) and (3), a person may apply for a termination order once they are absolutely discharged under paragraph 672.54(a).
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02912(3.1) (src:10553-10554)
GIVEN `they are absolutely discharged under paragraph 672.54(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02912(3.1) the person may apply for a termination order, despite subsections (2) and (3)` MEANS
    IF `they are absolutely discharged under paragraph 672.54(a)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person may apply for a termination order once they are absolutely discharged under paragraph 672.54(a)" [may-where] ("once" read as "when": ruling (b) of the periods ruling; name-test sweep of 2026-11-12)

-- src:10555 | Re-application
-- src:10556 | (4) A person whose application is refused may apply again if five years have elapsed since the application was made.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02912(4) (src:10555-10556)
GIVEN `their application is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which they apply again` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02912(4) the person may apply again for a termination order` MEANS
    IF `their application is refused` AND `the day on which they apply again` AT LEAST `s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which the application was made` 5
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person whose application is refused may apply again if five years have elapsed since the application was made" (fork F5)

§ `490.02913 Termination order`

-- src:10557 | Termination order
-- src:10558 | 490.02913 (1) The court shall make an order terminating the obligation if it is satisfied that the person has established that
-- src:10559 | (a) there would be no connection between continuing the obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act; or
-- src:10560 | (b) the impact of continuing the obligation on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02913(1) (src:10557-10560)
DECLARE `s 490.02913(1) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.02913(1) make an order terminating the obligation`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02913(1) (src:10557-10560)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the person has established that there would be no connection between continuing the obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of continuing the obligation on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02913(1) the court shall make an order terminating the obligation` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the person has established that there would be no connection between continuing the obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`
       OR `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of continuing the obligation on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall make an order terminating the obligation if it is satisfied that the person has established that" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02913(1) (src:10557-10560)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.02913(1) action`
`s 490.02913(1) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.02913(1) make an order terminating the obligation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court was satisfied of a ground and did not make an order terminating the obligation"

-- src:10561 | Factors
-- src:10562 | (1.1) In determining whether to make the termination order, the court shall consider
-- src:10563 | (a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation;
-- src:10564 | (b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics;
-- src:10565 | (c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim;
-- src:10566 | (d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person;
-- src:10567 | (e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence;
-- src:10568 | (f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person; and
-- src:10569 | (g) any other factors that the court considers relevant.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02913(1.1) (src:10561-10569)
DECLARE `s 490.02913(1.1) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.02913(1.1)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation`
    `s 490.02913(1.1)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics`
    `s 490.02913(1.1)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim`
    `s 490.02913(1.1)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person`
    `s 490.02913(1.1)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence`
    `s 490.02913(1.1)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person`
    `s 490.02913(1.1)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant`
    `s 490.02913(1.1) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02913(1.1) (src:10561-10569)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether to make the termination order` IS A BOOLEAN
      factor IS A `s 490.02913(1.1) factor`
      `the court considers the matter relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02913(1.1) the court shall consider the factor` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court is determining whether to make the termination order`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In determining whether to make the termination order, the court shall consider" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE CONSIDER factor
         WHEN `s 490.02913(1.1)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.02913(1.1)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.02913(1.1)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.02913(1.1)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.02913(1.1)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.02913(1.1)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.02913(1.1)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (g): "any other factors that the court considers relevant" is itself in the list
         WHEN `s 490.02913(1.1) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)` THEN IF `the court considers the matter relevant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only factors "that the court considers relevant" are added by paragraph (g)

-- src:10570 | Reasons for decision
-- src:10571 | (2) The court shall give reasons for its decision.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02913(2) (src:10570-10571)
DECLARE `s 490.02913(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.02913(2) give reasons for its decision`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02913(2) (src:10570-10571)
GIVEN `the court has made a decision under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02913(2) the court shall give reasons for its decision` MEANS
    IF `the court has made a decision under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "The court shall give reasons for its decision"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02913(2) (src:10570-10571)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.02913(2) action`
`s 490.02913(2) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.02913(2) give reasons for its decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not give reasons for its decision"

-- src:10572 | Requirements relating to notice
-- src:10573 | (3) If the court makes a termination order, it shall cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, to be notified of the decision.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02913(3) (src:10572-10573)
DECLARE `s 490.02913(3) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.02913(3) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, to be notified of the decision`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02913(3) (src:10572-10573)
GIVEN `the court makes a termination order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02913(3) the court shall cause the notification to be given` MEANS
    IF `the court makes a termination order` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court makes a termination order" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02913(3) (src:10572-10573)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.02913(3) action`
`s 490.02913(3) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.02913(3) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, to be notified of the decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court made a termination order and did not cause the notification to be given"

§ `490.02914 Appeal`

-- src:10574 | Appeal
-- src:10575 | 490.02914 (1) The Attorney General or the person who applied for a termination order may appeal from a decision under subsection 490.02913(1) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may dismiss the appeal, allow the appeal and order a new hearing, quash the termination order or make an order that may be made under that subsection.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02914(1) (src:10574-10575)
DECLARE `s 490.02914(1) appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.02914(1) the Attorney General`
    `s 490.02914(1) the person who applied for a termination order`
    `s 490.02914(1) another person`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02914(1) (src:10574-10575)
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 490.02914(1) appellant`
      `the decision appealed from is a decision under subsection 490.02913(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground of appeal raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02914(1) the appeal may be brought` MEANS
    IF appellant EQUALS `s 490.02914(1) another person` OR (NOT `the decision appealed from is a decision under subsection 490.02913(1)`) OR (NOT `the ground of appeal raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Attorney General or the person who applied for a termination order may appeal from a decision under subsection 490.02913(1) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10575 | 490.02914 (1) The Attorney General or the person who applied for a termination order may appeal from a decision under subsection 490.02913(1) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may dismiss the appeal, allow the appeal and order a new hearing, quash the termination order or make an order that may be made under that subsection.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02914(1) (src:10575-10575)
DECLARE `s 490.02914(1) thing the appeal court does` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.02914(1) dismiss the appeal`
    `s 490.02914(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing`
    `s 490.02914(1) quash the termination order`
    `s 490.02914(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.02913(1)`
    `s 490.02914(1) another thing`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02914(1) (src:10575-10575)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 490.02914(1) thing the appeal court does`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02914(1) the appeal court may do it` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `s 490.02914(1) dismiss the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.02914(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.02914(1) quash the termination order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.02914(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.02913(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.02914(1) another thing` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The appeal court may dismiss the appeal, allow the appeal and order a new hearing, quash the termination order or make an order that may be made under that subsection"

